## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the ability to design verifiable, privacy-preserving aggregation systems with end-to-end integrity guarantees using non-interactive zero-knowledge proofs. Candidates should outline the complete architecture, data flows, and anti-tampering mechanisms required for secure distributed computation.

## Key Concepts
- Privacy-preserving aggregation with succinct non-interactive arguments of knowledge (SNARKs)
- Tamper-evident ledger chaining for auditability
- Replay protection through nonce management and commitment schemes
- Poisoning resistance in distributed share systems via consistency checks

## Code Example
```javascript
async function verifyProof(proof, publicInputs) {
  // SNARK verification stub
  // Validates that aggregate(sum of shares) == claimed_output
  // without revealing individual share contributions
  return snarklib.verify(verificationKey, publicInputs, proof);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
1. How would you handle device dropout during aggregation rounds?
2. What fallback mechanisms exist if SNARK verification fails?
3. How do you calibrate proof generation time against aggregation freshness requirements?

## Why This Is Asked

Adds a practical multi-tenant privacy control layer to a beginner API, highlighting data isolation, per-tenant budgets, and simple governance in a real system.

## Key Concepts

- Multi-tenancy isolation
- Per-tenant privacy budgets (epsilon, delta)
- Header validation (X-tenant-id)
- Tenant-scoped configuration
- Observability and audits

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: tenant-aware config lookup (Express)
function tenantMiddleware(req, res, next) {
  const tenant = req.headers['x-tenant-id'];
  if (!tenant) return res.status(400).send('Missing X-tenant-id');
  req.tenant = loadTenantConfig(tenant); // returns {epsilon, delta, ...}
  if (!req.tenant) return res.status(403).send('Unknown tenant');
  next();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test for cross-tenant data leakage?
- How would you migrate tenants to per-tenant budgets with zero downtime?

## Why This Is Asked
Real-world federated privacy requires strict budget governance and data locality to satisfy regional compliance and tenant SLAs, while still enabling global analytics.

## Key Concepts
- Differential privacy budgets per tenant and per region
- Data locality constraints and secure regional processing
- Auditable, tamper-evident logs and rollback paths
- Lightweight per-tenant APIs for budget, policy, and audits

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple DP budget ledger update (conceptual)
function adjustBudget(tenant, epsDelta, deltaNotes){
  const rec = getBudget(tenant);
  rec.epsilon += epsDelta;
  rec.delta += deltaNotes?.delta || 0;
  saveBudget(tenant, rec);
  return rec;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
