## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates your ability to design governance-compliant, explainable ML systems for regulated fintech environments at scale.

## Key Concepts

- Policy engine with semantic versioning and rule inheritance
- Feature masking for privacy and regulatory compliance
- Explainability through SHAP values for auditability
- Distributed tracing with OpenTelemetry across the pipeline
- Automated drift detection and model monitoring
- Immutable audit trails with cryptographic verification
- Instant rollback mechanisms for policy changes

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode for policy-driven scoring workflow
function computeCCAScore(user, features, policyVersion) {
  const policy = getPolicyVersion(policyVersion);
  const allowedFeatures = policy.filterAllowed(features);
  const maskedFeatures = policy.maskSensitive(allowedFeatures, user);
  const explanation = computeSHAP(maskedFeatures, model);
  const auditTrail = createImmutableLog({user, policyVersion, timestamp});

  return {
    score: model.predict(maskedFeatures),
    explanation: explanation,
    policyVersion: policyVersion,
    auditId: auditTrail.id
  };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Interviewers want to see how a candidate reasons about privacy budgets, idempotency, and safe fallbacks in a real API flow—not just in theory.

## Key Concepts

- Privacy budget accounting and consumption tracking
- Atomic updates and concurrency safety
- Fallback mechanisms under budget constraints
- Replay protection (idempotency) and nonce handling
- Observability and auditing of budget usage

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example budget check and score computation
async function computeScore(userId, request) {
  const remaining = await budgetStore.get(userId) ?? DEFAULT_BUDGET;

  if (remaining < MIN_SAFE_BUDGET) {
    return {
      cca_score: computeHeuristicScore(userId),
      privacy_budget_remaining: remaining,
      budget_exhausted: true,
      fallback_heuristic: 'historical_average'
    };
  }

  const score = await computeWithModel(userId, request);
  const newBudget = remaining - EPSILON;
  await budgetStore.set(userId, newBudget);

  return {
    cca_score: score,
    privacy_budget_remaining: newBudget,
    budget_exhausted: false,
    fallback_heuristic: null
  };
}
```
